---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { t } from "../../i18n/ui";
import addressSvg from "../../assets/contact/address-en.svg?raw";
import emailSvg from "../../assets/contact/email.svg?raw";

const lang = "en";
---

<Layout
    title={t(lang, "nav.datenschutz")}
    lang="en"
    description="Privacy Policy of Jannik Menzel: Information about the handling of personal data on this website."
    keywords="Privacy, Privacy Policy, Jannik Menzel, Data, GDPR, Website"
    og={{
        title: `${t(lang, "nav.datenschutz")} – Jannik Menzel`,
        description:
            "Privacy Policy of Jannik Menzel: Information about the handling of personal data on this website.",
        url: "https://www.jannikmenzel.me/en/datenschutz/",
        image: "https://www.jannikmenzel.me/social-preview.png",
    }}
    twitter={{
        title: "Privacy Policy – Jannik Menzel",
        description: "Privacy policy of the website of Jannik Menzel.",
        image: "https://www.jannikmenzel.me/social-preview.png",
    }}
    canonical="https://www.jannikmenzel.me/en/datenschutz/"
    structuredData={{
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "WebPage",
        name: t(lang, "nav.datenschutz"),
        description:
            "Privacy Policy of Jannik Menzel: Information about the handling of personal data on this website.",
        url: "https://www.jannikmenzel.me/en/datenschutz/",
    }}
>
    <main class="w-full container px-4 sm:px-16 mb-22 max-w-[1100px]">
        <!-- Header -->
        <header class="pt-20">
            <h1 class="text-center text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold font-display mb-4">
                {t(lang, "nav.datenschutz")}
            </h1>
            <div class="h-1 w-24 bg-primary mx-auto"></div>
        </header>

        <!-- Content -->
        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6 pt-22">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2 flex justify-between items-baseline">
                <span>Introduction</span>
                <span class="text-base font-thin">Status: October 20, 2026</span>
            </h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                This privacy policy informs you about the type, scope and purpose of the processing
                of personal data (hereinafter "data") within my online offer and the associated
                websites, functions and content as well as external online presences, such as my
                social media profile. Data processing in the context of my freelance work (e.g.,
                quotes, projects and invoicing) is governed by a separate privacy policy that I
                provide to clients.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2">Privacy at a Glance</h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                Here you will find a brief overview of what happens to your personal data when you
                visit this website. Personal data is any data that can be used to personally
                identify you.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2">Who is responsible?</h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                The data processing on this website is carried out by me as the operator. Controller
                within the meaning of data protection laws:
            </p>

            <p class="font-thin text-justify mt-4 [hyphens:auto]">
                Jannik Menzel<br />
                <span class="block [&>svg]:block" set:html={addressSvg} />
                Email: <span class="inline-block align-top [&>svg]:block" set:html={emailSvg} />
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2">How is data collected?</h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                On the one hand, your data is collected by you providing it to me (e.g., via the
                contact form or by email). GitHub (hosting), Cloudflare and my own web analytics
                collect other data automatically when you visit the website, e.g., browser,
                operating system and time of the page request.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2">What is the data used for?</h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                Part of the data is collected to ensure the website functions without errors. Other
                data is used to process contact inquiries.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2">Purpose of Processing</h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                Processing is carried out to provide this website and my content, to answer contact
                inquiries, and to safeguard legitimate interests (e.g., security and operation of
                the website).
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2">Email Contact</h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                If you contact me by email, the personal data transmitted with your email (e.g.,
                name, email address, message) will be stored and processed for the purpose of
                handling your inquiry. The legal basis for this is Art. 6 Para. 1 lit. b GDPR
                insofar as the inquiry serves contract initiation or performance, as well as Art. 6
                Para. 1 lit. f GDPR based on the legitimate interest in responding to your inquiry.
                The data is deleted once your inquiry has been fully processed and no statutory
                retention obligations apply.
            </p>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify mt-4 [hyphens:auto]">
                To receive and store emails, I use the Private Email service of
                <strong>Namecheap, Inc.</strong> (4600 East Washington Street, Suite 300, Phoenix, AZ
                85034, USA). Emails sent to me and inquiries forwarded from the contact form are therefore
                stored on Namecheap's servers in the USA. The legal basis is Art. 6 Para. 1 lit. f GDPR.
                My legitimate interest lies in reliable email communication. The transfer to the USA is
                based on the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses (Art. 46 Para. 2 lit.
                c GDPR). For more information, please refer to
                <a
                    href="https://www.namecheap.com/legal/general/privacy-policy/"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline">Namecheap's Privacy Policy</a
                >.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2">Contact Form</h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                If you contact me via the contact form, the data you enter (e.g., name, email
                address, subject, message) will be processed for the purpose of handling your
                request and for possible follow-up questions. The legal basis is Art. 6 Para. 1 lit.
                b GDPR insofar as your inquiry relates to placing an order or an existing
                contractual relationship, and otherwise Art. 6 Para. 1 lit. f GDPR based on my
                legitimate interest in responding to your inquiry. The data is deleted once your
                inquiry has been fully processed and no statutory retention obligations apply.
            </p>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify mt-4 [hyphens:auto]">
                I process the form with <strong>n8n</strong>, automation software that I run myself.
                Your input is sent via HTTPS to a server I rent from Hetzner Online GmbH
                (Industriestr. 25, 91710 Gunzenhausen, Germany) and from there, encrypted, to my own
                server in Germany. There n8n checks it for completeness and spam and forwards it to
                my mailbox by email (see "Email Contact"). A data processing agreement pursuant to
                Art. 28 GDPR is in place with Hetzner. No other third parties receive any data. My
                server only keeps a request if forwarding fails, and then for no more than 14 days.
            </p>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify mt-4 [hyphens:auto]">
                When you submit the form, the servers involved log connection data (IP address,
                time, requested address, browser identifier). I use it only for security,
                troubleshooting and abuse prevention (Art. 6 Para. 1 lit. f GDPR) and delete it
                automatically after 14 days at the latest.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2">
                Hosting, Server Logs and Technical Data
            </h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                This website is hosted via <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> (a service of GitHub Inc., 88
                Colin P. Kelly Jr. St., San Francisco, CA 94107, USA). Each time the website is accessed,
                data is automatically collected in server log files, e.g., IP address, time of server
                request, referrer URL, browser used, and possibly accessed pages. This data is technically
                required to ensure stability and security of the page. The legal basis is Art. 6 Para.
                1 lit. f GDPR. My legitimate interest lies in the reliable and secure provision of this
                website. I have no access to these log data myself. GitHub stores them only as long as
                necessary for the purposes mentioned and deletes them afterwards. The use of GitHub Pages
                results in a transfer of data to the USA. GitHub Inc. is certified under the EU-US Data
                Privacy Framework (DPF), so an adequacy decision pursuant to Art. 45 GDPR applies to the
                data transfer. For more information, please refer to
                <a
                    href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline">GitHub's Privacy Policy</a
                >.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2">
                Content Delivery Network and Security (Cloudflare)
            </h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                This website uses the services of <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend
                St., San Francisco, CA 94107, USA). Cloudflare provides domain management (DNS) and acts
                as a reverse proxy and content delivery network (CDN) between your browser and the hosting
                at GitHub Pages. All requests to this website are therefore routed through Cloudflare's
                servers. In doing so, Cloudflare processes in particular your IP address, date and time
                of access, the requested URL, the referrer, and browser and system information. Cloudflare
                stores this data only as long as necessary for the purposes mentioned and deletes it in
                accordance with the periods stated in its privacy policy.
            </p>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify mt-4 [hyphens:auto]">
                Cloudflare is used to deliver the website quickly and reliably, to serve it
                encrypted (HTTPS), and to protect it against attacks (e.g., DDoS) and abusive
                access. To detect connection problems, your browser may also send technical error
                reports (e.g., on failed connections) to Cloudflare via the "Network Error Logging"
                feature. To fend off automated access, Cloudflare may set technically necessary
                cookies (e.g., <code>__cf_bm</code> or
                <code>cf_clearance</code>). These do not require consent pursuant to Section 25 (2)
                No. 2 TDDDG.
            </p>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify mt-4 [hyphens:auto]">
                The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) lit. f GDPR. My legitimate interest lies in the
                secure, stable and performant provision of this website. A data processing agreement
                (Data Processing Addendum) pursuant to Art. 28 GDPR is in place with Cloudflare.
                Processing may also take place in the USA. Cloudflare, Inc. is certified under the
                EU-US Data Privacy Framework (DPF), so an adequacy decision pursuant to Art. 45 GDPR
                applies to the data transfer. For more information, please refer to
                <a
                    href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="underline">Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a
                >.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2">
                Web Analytics (Plausible Analytics)
            </h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                For audience measurement, I use <strong>Plausible Analytics</strong> (Community Edition)
                on my own server in Germany. The script and measurement data travel via HTTPS through
                a server I rent from Hetzner Online GmbH (Industriestr. 25, 91710 Gunzenhausen, Germany),
                with which a data processing agreement pursuant to Art. 28 GDPR is in place. No other
                third parties receive any data. Plausible also determines the country locally. Plausible
                sets no cookies and stores no IP addresses. To count visitors, it creates a hash from
                the IP address and browser identifier using a key that changes daily, so you are not recognized
                the next day. Only aggregated data such as page visited, referrer, browser, operating
                system, device type and country is stored. The servers involved log connection data (IP
                address, time, requested address, browser identifier) and delete it after 14 days at the
                latest.
            </p>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto] mt-2">
                The legal basis is Art. 6 Para. 1 lit. f GDPR. My legitimate interest is to evaluate
                and improve my website in a data-minimizing way. You can prevent collection by
                disabling JavaScript or using a content blocker.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2">Your Rights</h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                You have the following rights with regard to the personal data concerning you: right
                of access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability,
                objection to processing, withdrawal of consent, and the right to lodge a complaint
                with a data protection supervisory authority.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2">
                RIGHT TO OBJECT PURSUANT TO ART. 21 GDPR
            </h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                <strong>a) Objection based on legitimate interests</strong><br />
                You have the right, on grounds relating to your particular situation, to object at any
                time to the processing of personal data concerning you that is carried out on the basis
                of Art. 6 Para. 1 lit. f GDPR (data processing based on a balancing of interests). This
                also applies to profiling based on this provision. If you object, I will no longer process
                your personal data unless I can demonstrate compelling legitimate grounds for the processing
                that override your interests, rights and freedoms, or the processing serves the establishment,
                exercise or defense of legal claims.
            </p>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify mt-4 [hyphens:auto]">
                <strong>b) Objection to direct marketing</strong><br />
                If I process your personal data for the purpose of direct marketing, you have the right
                to object at any time to the processing of personal data concerning you for such marketing
                purposes (Art. 21 Para. 2 GDPR). If you object, I will no longer process your personal
                data for direct marketing purposes.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2">Security</h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                I use technical and organizational security measures to protect your data against
                manipulation, loss, destruction, or unauthorized access by third parties.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-6 sm:mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium mb-2">Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
            <p class="font-thin text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                I reserve the right to adapt this privacy policy if necessary. The current version
                will be published on this page.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            <p class="text-justify [hyphens:auto]">
                For privacy-related questions, please use the contact form on the website or write
                an email to the address provided in the imprint.
            </p>
        </section>
    </main>
</Layout>
